  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'how to pick chicks' because the meme uses this phrase to create a dehumanizing and offensive analogy. The user is implicitly invited to imagine themselves as the one 'picking chicks' in Auschwitz, thereby internalizing the hateful metaphor and projecting their own identity onto the act of trivializing genocide. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the meme's structure and intent force the viewer to identify with the act described in the text, making the user a participant in the hateful framing.",
